Direct3D 10: one sample means not multisampled

Direct3D gives SampleDesc.Count = 1 for every resource that is not multisampled, buffers
included, and the driver passed that on as the sample count. Gallium's convention for "not
multisampled" is zero. With virgl the count goes to the host as it is: virglrenderer 0.10
makes a multisample texture for a count of one and refuses a buffer with a count
("Multisample textures not 2D"), so no vertex buffer could be created.

diff -ru a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp
@@ -302,8 +302,12 @@
    templat.depth0     = pCreateResource->pMipInfoList[0].TexelDepth;
    templat.array_size = pCreateResource->ArraySize;
    templat.last_level = pCreateResource->MipLevels - 1;
-   templat.nr_samples = pCreateResource->SampleDesc.Count;
-   templat.nr_storage_samples = pCreateResource->SampleDesc.Count;
+   /* Direct3D says one sample for anything not multisampled, buffers included. Gallium's
+    * word for that is zero, and a host renderer that is asked for a one-sample resource makes
+    * a multisample texture, or refuses a buffer outright.
+    */
+   templat.nr_samples = pCreateResource->SampleDesc.Count > 1 ? pCreateResource->SampleDesc.Count : 0;
+   templat.nr_storage_samples = templat.nr_samples;
    templat.bind       = translate_resource_flags(pCreateResource->BindFlags);
    templat.usage      = translate_resource_usage(pCreateResource->Usage);
 
